data codex_supervised_turn_authority_note: String = "SUPERVISED-RUNNER REALIZATION (continuity receipt 2026-08-13). In-flight turns do NOT survive client death — tool calls execute in the local app-server process, so one supervised process must fence each WorkerTurn attempt. std.temporal_effect HeldLease is the execution lease — an issued LeaseEpoch (lease_key, resource_fingerprint, owner_fingerprint, generation) plus the observed reading of it; do not mint a parallel session carrier. Update the observation through held_lease_with_observed, never by respelling the epoch fields.\n\nTHREE LAYERS STAY SEPARATE (reviewer ruling):\n  durable goal — WorkerTurn reaching a terminal disposition with an observed head\n  execution lease — HeldLease over the supervised app-server process, fenced by generation\n  controller — belt tick reconciling desired vs observed thread state\n\nTHE TRAP: an abandoned turn leaves thread status idle with partial work on disk. Thread idle alone NEVER authorizes turn/start; turn identity plus a runner-written terminal receipt is required. CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt is written ONLY by the supervised runner when the process ends — nothing else writes one on crash.\n\nExactly-once: client_command_id is carried on the terminal receipt so a lost turn/start reply does not collapse into absent."

data codex_supervised_process_supervision_note: String = "PROCESS SUPERVISION (srv1 receipt 2026-08-13). The lease fences the bundled native executable from CodexRuntimeBundle projection — NEVER /usr/bin/codex, which is a Node shim that spawns the platform binary. Killing the shim orphans the agent and produces a false 'work continued' reading. thread/start and turn/start share one held-open app-server stdin session realized through host_effect_apply CodexSupervisedWorkerTurn (gunbc.codex_supervised_turn_run). In-flight turns do NOT survive process death; thread/resume is the recovery path on a surviving thread."

data codex_supervised_lease_selection_receipt_note: String = "OPERATOR RULING #8166 (2026-08-13). Disconnect branch settled by srv1 execution, not argument: killing the real app-server binary mid-turn stopped work at 2 of 8 files; the thread survived and thread/resume is the recovery path. Detached reconciliation is refuted; supervised HeldLease over the app-server process is the selected realization. Stay draft until a bounded wet turn returns CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt — the admission fold alone is not mergeable. Wet access is a bounded srv1 execution grant, not a standing child credential."

data codex_supervised_turn_wet_handoff_note: String = "BOUNDED WET HANDOFF — BISECT FIRST (srv1 OOM receipt 2026-08-14). Bisect entrypoints in dag/test/claim/codex_supervised_turn_wet_witness_test.dag are plain fn (NOT enrolled witnesses — admission gate refuses enrolled-with-zero-consumers). Operator runs under MemoryMax caps on srv1 only. Step 1: wet_committed_admitted_source_lock_admits (2G). Step 2b: wet_select_codex_exact_target_closure_only (2G). Step 2: wet_materialize_codex_runtime_bundle_only (8G). Full chain after materialize_codex_runtime_bundle fixed; then enroll via gunbc.explicit_witness_admission."

data codex_supervised_client_command_id_file_name: String = "/codex_supervised_client_command_id"

data codex_supervised_turn_generation_file_name: String = "/codex_supervised_turn_generation"

data codex_supervised_operator_verdict_note: String = "OPERATOR VERDICT #8166 (2026-08-16): RejectAndFinishNow on concat-built bash coprocess scaffold. codex_supervised_turn_script DELETED. Supervised turn executes only through host_effect_apply CodexSupervisedWorkerTurn + extdeps.llm.codex_app_server_stdio_session typed transport. PR stays draft until (1) hand-built JSON/sed shell path is gone — satisfied by deletion — and (2) wet CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt executes through the modeled route. Wet srv1 grant held until session driver lands."

data codex_supervised_thread_id_slot: NonEmptyStr = "GUNBC_SUPERVISED_THREAD_ID_SLOT" as NonEmptyStr
type CodexThreadActivity
  = CodexThreadAbsent
  | CodexThreadIdle
  | CodexThreadBusy
  | CodexThreadActivityUnobserved { reason: NonEmptyStr }

type CodexSupervisedTurnBinding {
  turn: WorkerTurn
  lease: HeldLease
  execution_policy: TemporalEffectPolicy
  standing_receipt: CodexAccountStandingReceipt?
}

type CodexSupervisedTurnBindingPrepare
  = CodexSupervisedTurnBindingPrepared { binding: CodexSupervisedTurnBinding }
  | CodexSupervisedTurnBindingPrepareRefused { reason: NonEmptyStr }

type CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt {
  binding: CodexSupervisedTurnBinding
  native_thread_id: NonEmptyStr?
  native_turn_id: NonEmptyStr?
  client_command_id: NonEmptyStr
  disposition: ProviderTurnDisposition
  wire_evidence: ProviderWireEvidenceReceipt?
}

type CodexTurnStartAdmission
  = CodexTurnStartAdmitted
  | CodexTurnStartRefusedDuplicateExecution { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | CodexTurnStartRefusedOutcomeUnobserved { reason: NonEmptyStr }

type CodexSupervisedGenerationRead
  = GenerationAbsent
  | GenerationRead { generation: Int }
  | GenerationStoreUnreadable { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | GenerationStoreMalformed { content: String }
  | GenerationStoreNegative { value: Int }

type CodexSupervisedTurnOutcome
  = CodexSupervisedTurnOk { receipt: CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt }
  | CodexSupervisedTurnRefused { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | CodexSupervisedTurnUnavailable { reason: NonEmptyStr, process: ProviderProcessReceipt }

type SupervisedRpcObservation
  = SupervisedRpcAbsent
  | SupervisedRpcOk { native_id: NonEmptyStr }
  | SupervisedRpcError { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | SupervisedRpcDuplicate { count: Int }

type SupervisedTurnTerminalSignal
  = SupervisedTurnTerminalAbsent
  | SupervisedTurnTerminalCompleted
  | SupervisedTurnTerminalFailed { reason: NonEmptyStr }

// unreadable_lines COUNTS WHAT THE FOLD COULD NOT READ, because the alternative was to drop it.
// absorb_supervised_turn_line previously answered `acc` for a line parse_json refused: the line
// vanished, the accumulator advanced, and nothing anywhere recorded that a line had been lost. A
// stream of wholly unreadable lines then reached disposition_from_supervised_parse looking exactly
// like a stream that carried no terminal event.
//
// An EMPTY line is not counted and never was -- absorb_supervised_turn_line tests for it before
// parsing, and a blank line between records is ordinary stream shape rather than a failure. That
// distinction already existed and is preserved deliberately; only the unparseable arm changed.
type SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
  thread_start: SupervisedRpcObservation
  turn_start: SupervisedRpcObservation
  turn_terminal: SupervisedTurnTerminalSignal
  unreadable_lines: Int
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_lease_key(attempt_key: AttemptKey, turn_key: String) -> NonEmptyStr {
  concat(attempt_key, concat("/", turn_key)) as NonEmptyStr
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_resource_fingerprint(
  credential: AmbientCodexCredentialContext,
  attempt_key: AttemptKey,
) -> ContentHash {
  content_hash_of_value(
    value: join([credential.codex_home as String, attempt_key], "|"),
  )
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_owner_fingerprint(turn: WorkerTurn) -> ContentHash {
  content_hash_of_value(
    value: codex_supervised_turn_client_command_id(turn: turn) as String,
  )
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_session_policy(lease_key: NonEmptyStr) -> TemporalEffectPolicy {
  HeldSessionLease { lease_key: lease_key }
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_client_command_id(turn: WorkerTurn) -> NonEmptyStr {
  concat(turn.attempt_key, concat("/", turn.turn_key)) as NonEmptyStr
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_binding(
  turn: WorkerTurn,
  credential: AmbientCodexCredentialContext,
  prior_generation: Int,
  observed: HeldLeaseObservedState,
  standing_receipt: CodexAccountStandingReceipt?,
) -> CodexSupervisedTurnBinding {
  let lease_key = codex_supervised_turn_lease_key(
    attempt_key: turn.attempt_key,
    turn_key: turn.turn_key,
  )
  CodexSupervisedTurnBinding {
    turn: turn,
    lease: held_lease(
      epoch: LeaseEpoch {
        lease_key: lease_key,
        resource_fingerprint: codex_supervised_turn_resource_fingerprint(
          credential: credential,
          attempt_key: turn.attempt_key,
        ),
        owner_fingerprint: codex_supervised_turn_owner_fingerprint(turn: turn),
        generation: prior_generation + 1,
      },
      observed: observed,
    ),
    execution_policy: codex_supervised_turn_session_policy(lease_key: lease_key),
    standing_receipt: standing_receipt,
  }
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_binding_with_observed(
  binding: CodexSupervisedTurnBinding,
  observed: HeldLeaseObservedState,
) -> CodexSupervisedTurnBinding {
  CodexSupervisedTurnBinding {
    turn: binding.turn,
    lease: held_lease_with_observed(lease: binding.lease, observed: observed),
    execution_policy: binding.execution_policy,
    standing_receipt: binding.standing_receipt,
  }
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_client_command_id_store_path(evidence_root: FilePath) -> String {
  concat(evidence_root as String, codex_supervised_client_command_id_file_name)
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_generation_store_path(evidence_root: FilePath) -> String {
  concat(evidence_root as String, codex_supervised_turn_generation_file_name)
}

fn codex_supervised_generation_read_from_content(content: String) -> CodexSupervisedGenerationRead {
  let trimmed = trim(s: content)
  if trimmed == "" {
    GenerationStoreMalformed { content: content }
  } else {
    match parse_int(s: trimmed) {
      Absent => GenerationStoreMalformed { content: content }
      Present { value: n } =>
        if n >= 0 {
          GenerationRead { generation: n }
        } else {
          GenerationStoreNegative { value: n }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn codex_supervised_generation_read_from_store(
  store_present: Bool,
  read_success: Bool,
  content: String,
) -> CodexSupervisedGenerationRead {
  if store_present == false {
    GenerationAbsent
  } else if read_success == false {
    GenerationStoreUnreadable {
      reason: "supervised turn generation store unreadable" as NonEmptyStr,
    }
  } else {
    codex_supervised_generation_read_from_content(content: content)
  }
}

fn read_codex_supervised_turn_prior_generation(evidence_root: FilePath) -> CodexSupervisedGenerationRead {
  let path = codex_supervised_turn_generation_store_path(evidence_root: evidence_root)
  if shell.Test.IsFile(path: path as FilePath).is_file == false {
    GenerationAbsent
  } else {
    let read = Filesystem.Read(path: path)
    codex_supervised_generation_read_from_store(
      store_present: true,
      read_success: read.success,
      content: read.content,
    )
  }
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_generation_admission(
  read: CodexSupervisedGenerationRead,
) -> CodexTurnStartAdmission {
  match read {
    GenerationAbsent => CodexTurnStartAdmitted
    GenerationRead { generation: _ } => CodexTurnStartAdmitted
    GenerationStoreUnreadable { reason: r } =>
      CodexTurnStartRefusedDuplicateExecution { reason: r }
    GenerationStoreMalformed { content: c } =>
      CodexTurnStartRefusedDuplicateExecution {
        reason: concat("generation store malformed: ", c) as NonEmptyStr,
      }
    GenerationStoreNegative { value: v } =>
      CodexTurnStartRefusedDuplicateExecution {
        reason: concat("generation store negative: ", to_string(n: v)) as NonEmptyStr,
      }
  }
}

fn persist_codex_supervised_turn_generation(
  evidence_root: FilePath,
  generation: Int,
) -> Bool {
  Filesystem.Write(
    path: codex_supervised_turn_generation_store_path(evidence_root: evidence_root),
    content: to_string(n: generation),
  ).success
}

fn persist_codex_supervised_turn_client_command_id(
  evidence_root: FilePath,
  client_command_id: NonEmptyStr,
) -> Bool {
  Filesystem.Write(
    path: codex_supervised_turn_client_command_id_store_path(evidence_root: evidence_root),
    content: client_command_id as String,
  ).success
}

fn prepare_codex_supervised_turn_binding(
  turn: WorkerTurn,
  credential: AmbientCodexCredentialContext,
  evidence_root: FilePath,
  observed: HeldLeaseObservedState,
  standing_receipt: CodexAccountStandingReceipt?,
) -> CodexSupervisedTurnBindingPrepare {
  let generation_read = read_codex_supervised_turn_prior_generation(evidence_root: evidence_root)
  match codex_supervised_turn_generation_admission(read: generation_read) {
    CodexTurnStartAdmitted => {
      let prior_generation = match generation_read {
        GenerationAbsent => 0
        GenerationRead { generation: g } => g
        _ => 0
      }
      CodexSupervisedTurnBindingPrepared {
        binding: codex_supervised_turn_binding(
          turn: turn,
          credential: credential,
          prior_generation: prior_generation,
          observed: observed,
          standing_receipt: standing_receipt,
        ),
      }
    }
    CodexTurnStartRefusedDuplicateExecution { reason: r } =>
      CodexSupervisedTurnBindingPrepareRefused { reason: r }
    CodexTurnStartRefusedOutcomeUnobserved { reason: r } =>
      CodexSupervisedTurnBindingPrepareRefused { reason: r }
  }
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_session_standing_admits(
  classification: AccountStandingClassification,
) -> Bool {
  match classification {
    AccountStandingAuthenticatedRateLimitsReadable => true
    AccountStandingLoginRequired => false
    AccountStandingQuotaReached => false
    AccountStandingInitializeMissing => false
    AccountStandingIncomplete => false
  }
}

fn codex_turn_start_admission(
  terminal_receipt: CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt?,
  thread: CodexThreadActivity,
) -> CodexTurnStartAdmission {
  match thread {
    CodexThreadBusy =>
      CodexTurnStartRefusedOutcomeUnobserved {
        reason: "thread reports a turn in flight; await runner terminal receipt" as NonEmptyStr,
      }
    CodexThreadActivityUnobserved { reason: r } =>
      CodexTurnStartRefusedOutcomeUnobserved { reason: r }
    CodexThreadAbsent => CodexTurnStartAdmitted
    CodexThreadIdle =>
      match terminal_receipt {
        Absent =>
          CodexTurnStartRefusedDuplicateExecution {
            reason: "thread idle without runner terminal receipt; partial work may exist on disk" as NonEmptyStr,
          }
        Present { value: receipt } =>
          if press_display_finished(disposition: receipt.disposition) {
            CodexTurnStartAdmitted
          } else {
            CodexTurnStartRefusedOutcomeUnobserved {
              reason: "prior turn lacks a finished terminal disposition from the runner" as NonEmptyStr,
            }
          }
      }
  }
}

fn provider_standing_bundle_from_codex_supervised_binding(
  binding: CodexSupervisedTurnBinding,
) -> ProviderStandingBundle? {
  match binding.standing_receipt {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: receipt } =>
      Present {
        value: provider_standing_bundle_from_codex_press_receipt(receipt: receipt),
      }
  }
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_start_line_template(user_input: String) -> String {
  codex_app_server_turn_start_request_line(
    thread_id: codex_supervised_thread_id_slot,
    user_input: user_input,
  ) as String
}

// FOUR CAUSES BEHIND ONE `none`, AND THE LAST ARM WAS A WILDCARD OVER A COPRODUCT WHOSE VARIANTS
// HAVE DIFFERENT REMEDIES -- the shape DESIGN names as total at the level examined, blind one level
// down. `_ => none` was exhaustive over SupervisedRpcObservation and said nothing about the
// distinction that decides what to do: an RPC ERROR is the provider refusing our thread-start, a
// DUPLICATE is two responses claiming the same id (a protocol violation on the wire), and neither
// is "this line was not the thread-start response", which is the ordinary, expected answer while
// scanning a stream.
//
// At an Optional that collapse is the worse one: a scanner looking for the thread id gets `none`
// for the line it should skip AND for the provider having refused, so a supervised run whose
// thread-start was rejected looks exactly like one whose response has not arrived yet.
type SupervisedThreadIdReading
  = ThreadIdRead { id: NonEmptyStr }
  | ThreadIdLineBlank
  | ThreadIdLineUnreadable
  | ThreadIdRpcRefused { reason: NonEmptyStr }
  | ThreadIdRpcDuplicated { count: Int }
  | ThreadIdLineNotThreadStart

// THE not-this-line ARM EXISTS AND IS UNPRODUCIBLE TODAY, AND THAT IS A REPORTED DEFECT RATHER
// THAN AN OVERSIGHT.
//
// Writing this vocabulary surfaced it: supervised_rpc_from_id_response takes `id: Int` and NEVER
// INSPECTS THE id MEMBER OF THE DOCUMENT -- the parameter is used only to build message text. So
// any well-formed response carrying result.<entity>.id is read as the thread-start response
// whatever id it is answering, and SupervisedRpcAbsent is unreachable from that function.
//
// The arm is kept rather than folded into a neighbour, because mapping "this line was addressed
// elsewhere" onto ThreadIdLineUnreadable would be the state-space conflation this whole change is
// removing -- it would put a lie in the decoder to avoid an unreachable arm. What is NOT done is
// write a witness for it: its RED is unauthorable today, and DESIGN section 4b rules such a probe
// worse than absent because it is cited as coverage. Exhaustiveness requires the arm; evidence does
// not exist for it, and the difference is stated rather than papered over.
//
// The mis-addressed-response class is NOT repaired here -- it is an id-matching defect, not a
// parse_json fail-open, and repairing it silently inside a decoder-honesty pass would be the
// widening this pass exists to stop doing. Its NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER is the id check landing in
// supervised_rpc_from_id_response, at which point this arm becomes producible and gets its witness.
// It is witnessed at its CURRENT behaviour in the witness module, so that fix turns that witness
// red at the line explaining why.
fn supervised_thread_id_from_line(line: String) -> SupervisedThreadIdReading {
  let trimmed = line.trim()
  if trimmed == "" {
    ThreadIdLineBlank
  } else {
    match parse_json(s: trimmed) {
      Absent => ThreadIdLineUnreadable
      Present { value: parsed } =>
        match supervised_rpc_from_id_response(
          id: codex_supervised_thread_start_id,
          obj: parsed,
          entity_key: codex_thread_start_result_thread_key as String,
        ) {
          SupervisedRpcOk { native_id: id } => ThreadIdRead { id: id }
          SupervisedRpcError { reason: reason } => ThreadIdRpcRefused { reason: reason }
          SupervisedRpcDuplicate { count: count } => ThreadIdRpcDuplicated { count: count }
          SupervisedRpcAbsent => ThreadIdLineNotThreadStart
        }
    }
  }
}

fn native_id_from_entity_result(result: JsonValue, entity_key: String) -> NonEmptyStr? {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: result, key: entity_key) {
    JsonMemberFound { value: entity } =>
      match entity {
        JsonObject { members: _ } =>
          match json_object_unique_member(
            v: entity,
            key: codex_entity_id_key as String,
          ) {
            JsonMemberFound { value: JsonString { value: id } } =>
              if id == "" {
                none
              } else {
                Present { value: id as NonEmptyStr }
              }
            _ => none
          }
        _ => none
      }
    _ => none
  }
}

fn supervised_rpc_from_id_response(
  id: Int,
  obj: JsonValue,
  entity_key: String,
) -> SupervisedRpcObservation {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: obj, key: "error") {
    JsonMemberFound { value: err } =>
      SupervisedRpcError {
        reason: concat(
          "json-rpc error on id ",
          concat(to_string(n: id), concat(": ", serialize_supervised_rpc_error(err: err))),
        ) as NonEmptyStr,
      }
    JsonMemberAbsent =>
      match json_object_unique_member(v: obj, key: "result") {
        JsonMemberFound { value: result } =>
          match native_id_from_entity_result(result: result, entity_key: entity_key) {
            Present { value: native_id } => SupervisedRpcOk { native_id: native_id }
            Absent =>
              SupervisedRpcError {
                reason: concat(
                  "id ",
                  concat(
                    to_string(n: id),
                    concat(": result missing ", concat(entity_key, " id")),
                  ),
                ) as NonEmptyStr,
              }
          }
        JsonMemberAbsent =>
          SupervisedRpcError {
            reason: concat("id ", concat(to_string(n: id), ": missing result")) as NonEmptyStr,
          }
        JsonMemberDuplicated { count: _ } =>
          SupervisedRpcError {
            reason: concat("id ", concat(to_string(n: id), ": duplicate result")) as NonEmptyStr,
          }
        JsonMemberNotAnObject =>
          SupervisedRpcError {
            reason: concat("id ", concat(to_string(n: id), ": result not object")) as NonEmptyStr,
          }
      }
    JsonMemberDuplicated { count: _ } =>
      SupervisedRpcError {
        reason: concat("id ", concat(to_string(n: id), ": duplicate error")) as NonEmptyStr,
      }
    JsonMemberNotAnObject =>
      SupervisedRpcError {
        reason: concat("id ", concat(to_string(n: id), ": error not object")) as NonEmptyStr,
      }
  }
}

fn serialize_supervised_rpc_error(err: JsonValue) -> String {
  match err {
    JsonObject { members: _ } => "structured error" as String
    JsonNull => "unstructured error" as String
    JsonBool { value: _ } => "unstructured error" as String
    JsonNumber { lexeme: _ } => "unstructured error" as String
    JsonString { value: _ } => "unstructured error" as String
    JsonArray { elements: _ } => "unstructured error" as String
  }
}

fn supervised_turn_terminal_from_notification(parsed: JsonValue) -> SupervisedTurnTerminalSignal {
  match json_object_unique_member(v: parsed, key: "method") {
    JsonMemberFound { value: JsonString { value: method } } =>
      if method == "turn/completed" {
        SupervisedTurnTerminalCompleted
      } else if method == "turn/failed" {
        SupervisedTurnTerminalFailed {
          reason: "turn/failed notification" as NonEmptyStr,
        }
      } else {
        SupervisedTurnTerminalAbsent
      }
    _ => SupervisedTurnTerminalAbsent
  }
}

fn absorb_supervised_rpc(
  current: SupervisedRpcObservation,
  next: SupervisedRpcObservation,
) -> SupervisedRpcObservation {
  match current {
    SupervisedRpcAbsent => next
    SupervisedRpcOk { native_id: _ } =>
      SupervisedRpcDuplicate { count: 2 }
    SupervisedRpcError { reason: _ } =>
      SupervisedRpcDuplicate { count: 2 }
    SupervisedRpcDuplicate { count: c } => SupervisedRpcDuplicate { count: c + 1 }
  }
}

fn absorb_supervised_turn_line(
  acc: SupervisedTurnParseAcc,
  line: String,
) -> SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
  let trimmed = line.trim()
  if trimmed == "" {
    acc
  } else {
    match parse_json(s: trimmed) {
      Absent =>
        SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
          thread_start: acc.thread_start,
          turn_start: acc.turn_start,
          turn_terminal: acc.turn_terminal,
          unreadable_lines: acc.unreadable_lines + 1,
        }
      Present { value: parsed } =>
        match json_object_unique_member(v: parsed, key: "id") {
          JsonMemberFound { value: idv } =>
            match json_rpc_id_as_int(v: idv) {
              Present { value: n } =>
                if n == codex_supervised_thread_start_id {
                  SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
                    thread_start: absorb_supervised_rpc(
                      current: acc.thread_start,
                      next: supervised_rpc_from_id_response(
                        id: n,
                        obj: parsed,
                        entity_key: codex_thread_start_result_thread_key as String,
                      ),
                    ),
                    turn_start: acc.turn_start,
                    turn_terminal: acc.turn_terminal,
                    unreadable_lines: acc.unreadable_lines,
                  }
                } else if n == codex_supervised_turn_start_wire_id {
                  SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
                    thread_start: acc.thread_start,
                    turn_start: absorb_supervised_rpc(
                      current: acc.turn_start,
                      next: supervised_rpc_from_id_response(
                        id: n,
                        obj: parsed,
                        entity_key: codex_turn_start_result_turn_key as String,
                      ),
                    ),
                    turn_terminal: acc.turn_terminal,
                    unreadable_lines: acc.unreadable_lines,
                  }
                } else {
                  acc
                }
              Absent =>
                match supervised_turn_terminal_from_notification(parsed: parsed) {
                  SupervisedTurnTerminalAbsent => acc
                  signal =>
                    SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
                      thread_start: acc.thread_start,
                      turn_start: acc.turn_start,
                      turn_terminal: signal,
                      unreadable_lines: acc.unreadable_lines,
                    }
                }
            }
          _ =>
            match supervised_turn_terminal_from_notification(parsed: parsed) {
              SupervisedTurnTerminalAbsent => acc
              signal =>
                SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
                  thread_start: acc.thread_start,
                  turn_start: acc.turn_start,
                  turn_terminal: signal,
                  unreadable_lines: acc.unreadable_lines,
                }
            }
        }
    }
  }
}

fn json_rpc_id_as_int(v: JsonValue) -> Int? {
  match v {
    JsonNumber { lexeme: l } => parse_int(s: l as String)
    JsonNull => none
    JsonBool { value: _ } => none
    JsonString { value: _ } => none
    JsonArray { elements: _ } => none
    JsonObject { members: _ } => none
  }
}

fn empty_supervised_turn_parse_acc() -> SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
  SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
    thread_start: SupervisedRpcAbsent,
    turn_start: SupervisedRpcAbsent,
    turn_terminal: SupervisedTurnTerminalAbsent,
    unreadable_lines: 0,
  }
}

fn parse_supervised_turn_stdout(stdout: String) -> SupervisedTurnParseAcc {
  fold(
    split(s: stdout, delimiter: "\n"),
    init: empty_supervised_turn_parse_acc(),
    f: (acc, line) => absorb_supervised_turn_line(acc: acc, line: line),
  )
}

// A NONZERO EXIT STILL REPORTS FAILURE EVEN WHEN LINES WERE UNREADABLE, and that ordering is a
// judgement rather than an oversight. A process that exited nonzero has told us something about
// ITSELF, from outside our decoder; our inability to read its stdout does not weaken that. The
// unreadable check therefore guards only the two arms that would otherwise answer NotObserved --
// the arms that assert an ABSENCE this build is no longer entitled to assert.
fn disposition_from_supervised_parse(
  parse: SupervisedTurnParseAcc,
  exit_code: Int?,
) -> ProviderTurnDisposition {
  match parse.turn_terminal {
    SupervisedTurnTerminalCompleted => ProviderTurnCompleted
    SupervisedTurnTerminalFailed { reason: r } =>
      ProviderTurnFailed {
        cause: ProviderNativeCauseUnknown { evidence: r },
      }
    SupervisedTurnTerminalAbsent =>
      match exit_code {
        Present { value: code } =>
          if code == 0 {
            if parse.unreadable_lines > 0 {
              ProviderTurnStreamUnreadable { unreadable_lines: parse.unreadable_lines }
            } else {
              ProviderTurnNotObserved
            }
          } else {
            ProviderTurnFailed {
              cause: ProviderNativeCauseUnknown {
                evidence: concat(
                  "app-server exited ",
                  to_string(n: code),
                  "",
                ) as NonEmptyStr,
              },
            }
          }
        Absent =>
          if parse.unreadable_lines > 0 {
            ProviderTurnStreamUnreadable { unreadable_lines: parse.unreadable_lines }
          } else {
            ProviderTurnNotObserved
          }
      }
  }
}

fn codex_runner_turn_terminal_receipt(
  binding: CodexSupervisedTurnBinding,
  parse: SupervisedTurnParseAcc,
  disposition: ProviderTurnDisposition,
  wire: ProviderWireEvidenceReceipt?,
) -> CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt {
  CodexRunnerTurnTerminalReceipt {
    binding: binding,
    native_thread_id: match parse.thread_start {
      SupervisedRpcOk { native_id: id } => Present { value: id }
      _ => none
    },
    native_turn_id: match parse.turn_start {
      SupervisedRpcOk { native_id: id } => Present { value: id }
      _ => none
    },
    client_command_id: codex_supervised_turn_client_command_id(turn: binding.turn),
    disposition: disposition,
    wire_evidence: wire,
  }
}

fn codex_supervised_turn_outcome_from_capture(
  running_binding: CodexSupervisedTurnBinding,
  stdout: String,
  stderr: String,
  exit_code: Int?,
  wire: ProviderWireEvidenceReceipt?,
  evidence_root: FilePath,
) -> CodexSupervisedTurnOutcome {
  let session_standing = parse_account_trip_session(
    stdout: stdout,
    stderr: stderr,
    evidence_root: evidence_root,
    mode: AccountTripDigestRetainPrivateSha512,
  )
  if codex_supervised_turn_session_standing_admits(
    classification: session_standing.classification,
  ) == false {
    CodexSupervisedTurnRefused {
      reason: "in-session account/rateLimits standing not readable" as NonEmptyStr,
    }
  } else {
    let parse = parse_supervised_turn_stdout(stdout: stdout)
    let disposition = disposition_from_supervised_parse(
      parse: parse,
      exit_code: exit_code,
    )
    let terminal_binding = codex_supervised_turn_binding_with_observed(
      binding: running_binding,
      observed: LeaseAbsent,
    )
    if persist_codex_supervised_turn_generation(
      evidence_root: evidence_root,
      generation: terminal_binding.lease.epoch.generation,
    ) == false {
      CodexSupervisedTurnRefused {
        reason: "failed to persist supervised turn generation fence" as NonEmptyStr,
      }
    } else {
      let receipt = codex_runner_turn_terminal_receipt(
        binding: terminal_binding,
        parse: parse,
        disposition: disposition,
        wire: wire,
      )
      CodexSupervisedTurnOk { receipt: receipt }
    }
  }
}
